[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]The EDGE quest maker for Cyberpunk 2077, in VS Code.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center]Read any of the game's quests in plain words: its steps, its choices, who says what and what goes in the journal. Then write your own as a short story, and EDGEquest makes the game's quest files from it: the phase, the journal, the scenes and their texts.[/center]
[center][/center]
[center][color=#f6b26b][size=3][i]An early preview: small quests with V, choices and branches, tested in the game.[/i][/size][/color][/center]
[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]STATUS: PREVIEW[/color][/b][/size]
What is here works and is tested in the game. New features land in small updates.
[b]This is not a game mod.[/b] It is an extension for VS Code, so install it there (steps below), not with Vortex. The quickest way is straight from the [url=https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=edgemodders.edgequest]VS Code Marketplace[/url] or [url=https://open-vsx.org/extension/edgemodders/edgequest]Open VSX[/url]; the file here is the same extension.[/quote]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What EDGEquest is[/color][/b][/size]

EDGEquest is built by [url=https://edgemodders.ai/]EDGEmodders[/url], a modding community whose idea is simple: [b]anyone can mod[/b]. Quests are among the hardest things to mod in Cyberpunk 2077: graphs of nodes, facts, journal entries, scenes and their texts, all in binary files that must agree with each other. EDGEquest turns that into words. You read the game's quests as numbered steps, and you write a quest as a story: beats with objectives, places, and scenes with lines and choices.

It reads and writes the game's files through [b]REDbridge[/b], which runs [b]WolvenKit[/b]'s libraries, and it works with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35421]REDcode[/url], which packs and installs your quest. Credit for the file formats and years of research belongs to the WolvenKit team and the modding community.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Highlights[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Read the game's quests[/color][/b][/size]
Every quest, phase and scene in the game, in a tree titled with the quests' names. A quest page shows a quest or phase as numbered steps in plain words, with its facts, journal entries, scenes, phases, people and places; the phases and scenes it plays are links. A scene page shows who is in it, each line with its speaker and text, and each choice and where it leads. [b]Find Quest[/b] searches by in-game title, file name, fact, journal entry, person or place.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Write a quest as a story[/color][/b][/size]
[b]New Quest[/b] starts one in your WolvenKit project from a template that plays. A story file is a set of beats, each with a journal objective and steps: go to a place, play a scene, wait, set a fact, end the quest. A choice in a scene can send the quest to another beat, so it branches, and branches can join again. Endings succeed or fail.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]The Storyboard[/color][/b][/size]
Your quest as cards, one per beat, titled with its objective, with arrows labelled by the choice that leads there. Click a card for its page: its steps, its scenes' lines and choices, and how each line is spoken. Add and rename beats, send a choice to a beat, edit lines and options in place. Every change goes into the story file, comments kept.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Save, and the quest is made[/color][/b][/size]
Saving the story file makes the quest's game files: the quest phase, the journal, the scenes, the texts and the ArchiveXL file, checked against each other. Problems show in VS Code's Problems panel at their line. Pack and install with REDcode, and play it.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Places, choices, music and sound[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Places[/b] are map markers the game already has. The quest waits until V is inside the place's trigger area, as the game's own quests do.[/*]
[*][b]Choices[/b] can be yellow (they move the quest on), white, for one lifepath, an attribute check, or a payment that takes the eddies.[/*]
[*][b]Music and sound:[/b] start and stop the game's music cues, and play its sound events or your own sounds made with [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEwave]EDGEwave[/url], in a beat or between a scene's lines. The picker plays each one before you pick it.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]The checklist[/color][/b][/size]
What is still a stand-in, such as lines shown as text with no voice yet, is listed in the story file with the EDGE tool that can do it, and ticks itself when it is done.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Check a quest mod[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Check Quest Mod[/b] reads a quest mod's archive, WolvenKit project or extracted files, and names what is wrong in plain words: missing files, entries that point nowhere, texts that are not there.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]For AI assistants[/color][/b][/size]
[url=https://www.npmjs.com/package/@edgemodders/edgequest-mcp]@edgemodders/edgequest-mcp[/url] gives Claude Code and other assistants the same quest maker: read the game's quests, start a quest, change its story, make it, and work through its checklist.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Coming next[/color][/b][/size]
Planned: phone calls with game characters, copying a game scene into your quest, people standing in your scenes, and voiced lines in the game.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, and Cyberpunk 2077 2.5 on PC.[/*]
[*][url=https://code.visualstudio.com/]VS Code[/url] 1.70 or later, [url=https://vscodium.com/]VSCodium[/url], or EDGEkit.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35421]REDcode[/url]: it finds the game, installs REDbridge (0.11.0 or later) and the .NET 10 runtime, and packs and installs your quest.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4198]ArchiveXL[/url] in the game, for the quests you make.[/*]
[*]Optional: [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEwave]EDGEwave[/url] to find, hear and make sounds; [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode]REDnode[/url] to hear music in the running game.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[b]From a store (recommended, updates itself):[/b] in VS Code, open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X), search for [b]EDGEquest[/b] and click Install. Or open its [url=https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=edgemodders.edgequest]Marketplace[/url] or [url=https://open-vsx.org/extension/edgemodders/edgequest]Open VSX[/url] page.

[b]From the file here:[/b]
[list]
[*]Install REDcode first, from its page or a store.[/*]
[*]Download the main file with [b]Manual download[/b] and extract it anywhere.[/*]
[*]In VS Code, open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X), click [b]...[/b] at its top, choose [b]Install from VSIX...[/b] and pick [i]edgequest-<version>.vsix[/i].[/*]
[*]Click the EDGEquest icon in the activity bar.[/*]
[/list]
Do not install it with Vortex: it is not a game mod, and Vortex would put it in the game folder.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]The EDGE platform[/color][/b][/size]

EDGEquest is one of the EDGE tools. Each works on its own and together:

[list]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35421]REDcode[/url][/b]: the modding workspace in VS Code. It packs and installs your quest.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEwave]EDGEwave[/url][/b]: the sound studio. Sounds and, later, voices for your quest's lines.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEdeck]EDGEdeck[/url][/b]: a simple mod manager in VS Code, for installs you can undo.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode]REDnode[/url][/b]: mods in JavaScript and web pages over the game; it plays music in the running game for EDGEquest's picker.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDbridge]REDbridge[/url][/b]: runs WolvenKit's libraries for the EDGE tools.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Do I need to know how quests work inside?[/b]
No. You write beats, places, lines and choices; EDGEquest writes the nodes, facts and files. The raw files are one click away when you want to see them, in REDcode.

[b]Can people talk to V in my scenes?[/b]
Not yet. In this preview V talks alone and makes choices. People standing in a scene, phone calls and voiced lines are next.

[b]Will it change my game folder?[/b]
No. EDGEquest writes into your WolvenKit project. Your quest reaches the game only when you pack and install it with REDcode or EDGEdeck.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes, and open source under the MIT license. The code is on [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEquest]GitHub[/url].

